---
import Curve from "../../components/Curve.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import Starfield from "../../components/Starfield.astro";
import Navigation from "../../components/Navigation.astro";
import "../../css/reset.css";
import "../../css/global.css";
import "../../css/index.css";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="TypeScript monorepo and PostgreSQL consulting from an experienced software engineer. Expert guidance on monorepo architecture (Turborepo, Nx, pnpm workspaces), PostgreSQL schema design, query optimization, code review, and platform evaluation. Starting at $120/hour."
    />
    <meta
      property="og:title"
      content="TypeScript Monorepo & PostgreSQL Consulting | Starburst Digital"
    />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="TypeScript monorepo and PostgreSQL consulting. Expert guidance on Turborepo, Nx, pnpm workspaces, PostgreSQL schema design and query optimization. Starting at $120/hour. First consultation is free."
    />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
    <meta
      name="twitter:title"
      content="TypeScript Monorepo & PostgreSQL Consulting | Starburst Digital"
    />
    <meta
      name="twitter:description"
      content="TypeScript monorepo and PostgreSQL consulting. Expert guidance on Turborepo, Nx, pnpm workspaces, PostgreSQL schema design and query optimization. Starting at $120/hour."
    />
    <title>TypeScript Monorepo & PostgreSQL Consulting - Starburst Digital</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <Starfield>
      <header class="flow">
        <p class="wrapper mt-m-l">
          <a href="/" class="big-brand">Starburst Digital</a>
        </p>
        <nav style="padding-top:1px;padding-bottom:1px;">
          <Navigation />
        </nav>
      </header>
      <div class="section__inner">
        <div class="wrapper flow region">
          <h1>Technical Consulting</h1>
          <p class="big">
            I specialize in TypeScript monorepos and PostgreSQL — two
            technologies that large teams depend on and that are genuinely hard
            to get right. Whether you need architecture guidance, a code review,
            or a trusted second opinion, I offer hourly and project-based
            consulting that saves you from expensive mistakes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Starfield>

    <main>
      <article class="flow region wrapper">
        <h2>Pricing</h2>
        <div class="grid" data-layout="50-50">
          <div class="flow">
            <h3>Starting at $120/Hour</h3>
            <p>
              Flexible engagement models to fit your needs. Whether you need a
              quick code review, ongoing strategic guidance, or help with a
              specific project, I offer pricing options that make sense.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Hourly consulting</strong> is perfect for one-off questions,
              second opinions, or when you need expert input on a specific technical
              decision.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Weekly retainers and project-based pricing</strong> are available
              for ongoing engagements or larger projects, providing better value and
              predictable costs.
            </p>
            <p>
              <a href="/contact">Contact me</a> to discuss your specific needs and
              get a custom quote.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card flow">
            <h3>What You Get</h3>
            <ul class="flow" data-flow="sm">
              <li>Full access to my expertise and experience</li>
              <li>Strategic planning and recommendations</li>
              <li>Technology and platform guidance</li>
              <li>Ongoing support and advice</li>
              <li>Code review and architecture feedback</li>
              <li>Unbiased vendor and tool evaluations</li>
              <li>Follow-up support as your project evolves</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="flow region wrapper">
        <h2>Specialties</h2>
        <div class="grid" data-layout="50-50">
          <div class="card flow">
            <h3>TypeScript Monorepos</h3>
            <p>
              Monorepos are a powerful pattern for large teams, but they're
              notoriously painful to set up and maintain. Slow builds, tangled
              dependencies, inconsistent tooling — I've solved these problems
              before and can help you avoid them from the start.
            </p>
            <p>
              I have deep experience with the entire monorepo ecosystem:
              Turborepo, Nx, pnpm workspaces, Yarn workspaces, and the
              TypeScript project reference configurations that tie it all
              together. Whether you're migrating an existing multi-repo setup or
              architecting a new one, I'll help you build a codebase your team
              can actually work in.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card flow">
            <h3>PostgreSQL</h3>
            <p>
              PostgreSQL is used everywhere — and it's easy to use it wrong.
              Slow queries, poorly designed schemas, missing indexes, N+1
              problems — these issues compound over time and become expensive to
              fix once data grows.
            </p>
            <p>
              I can help with schema design and normalization, query
              optimization, index strategy, connection pooling, and migration
              planning. Whether you're starting fresh or inheriting a legacy
              database, I'll help you get PostgreSQL working for you instead of
              against you.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <div class="section spot-color-secondary">
        <Curve />
        <div class="section__inner">
          <article class="flow region wrapper">
            <h2>How It Works</h2>
            <p>
              Start with a free consultation. Tell me what you're working on —
              a problem you're stuck on, a decision you're weighing, or a system
              you need reviewed. I'll ask questions, give you my honest read on
              the situation, and let you know whether and how I can help.
            </p>
            <p>
              From there, we scope the engagement together. Some engagements are
              a single session to answer a specific question. Others are ongoing
              retainers where I'm available on a weekly basis. I'll recommend
              whatever structure actually fits your needs.
            </p>
            <p>
              No retainer required to get started. No sales pitch on the first
              call.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <Curve />
      </div>

      <article class="flow region wrapper">
        <h2>How I Can Help</h2>
        <ul class="grid" data-layout="50-50" role="list">
          <li class="card flow">
            <h3>Code Review & Audit</h3>
            <p>
              Get a second pair of eyes on your codebase. I'll identify security
              issues, performance bottlenecks, maintainability concerns, and
              provide actionable recommendations.
            </p>
            <p>
              Whether you're preparing for a launch, inheriting legacy code, or
              want to ensure your team is following best practices, a
              professional code review catches problems before they become
              expensive to fix.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="card flow">
            <h3>Platform Evaluation</h3>
            <p>
              Choosing between AWS, Vercel, and Netlify? React vs. Vue? MongoDB
              or PostgreSQL? I'll help you evaluate options based on your
              specific needs, not vendor marketing.
            </p>
            <p>
              Technology decisions have long-term consequences. I'll help you
              assess trade-offs, estimate costs, and choose platforms that align
              with your team's skills and your business goals.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="card flow">
            <h3>Monorepo Architecture</h3>
            <p>
              Design a TypeScript monorepo that scales with your team — fast
              builds, clear package boundaries, shared tooling, and a structure
              developers actually want to work in.
            </p>
            <p>
              I'll help you choose the right tools (Turborepo, Nx, pnpm
              workspaces), configure TypeScript project references correctly, and
              establish patterns for code sharing that don't create a tangled
              dependency mess down the road.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="card flow">
            <h3>Technical Due Diligence</h3>
            <p>
              Acquiring a company or evaluating a technology partner? I'll
              assess technical capabilities, code quality, infrastructure, and
              technical debt.
            </p>
            <p>
              Understanding the technical reality behind the pitch can save you
              from costly surprises. I provide thorough, honest assessments that
              help you make informed decisions.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="card flow">
            <h3>PostgreSQL Performance</h3>
            <p>
              Slow queries, runaway costs, or a schema that's started working
              against you? I'll identify the actual bottlenecks — missing
              indexes, inefficient queries, N+1 patterns — and fix them.
            </p>
            <p>
              I'll profile your queries with <code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code>,
              optimize index strategy, tune connection pooling, and make
              targeted changes that deliver measurable improvements without
              rewriting your entire data layer.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="card flow">
            <h3>Team Training & Mentorship</h3>
            <p>
              Level up your development team with targeted training on best
              practices, modern tools, security, testing, and software
              architecture.
            </p>
            <p>
              Investing in your team's skills pays long-term dividends. I offer
              practical, hands-on training tailored to your technology stack and
              business needs—not generic tutorials.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <div class="section spot-color-primary">
        <Curve />
        <div class="section__inner">
          <article class="flow region wrapper">
            <h2>Who I Work With</h2>
            <p>
              I work with startups, small businesses, and growing companies who
              need senior-level technical expertise without hiring full-time.
            </p>
            <p>
              Whether you're a non-technical founder trying to make smart
              technology choices, a small development team that needs strategic
              guidance, or a business evaluating a technical acquisition, I can
              help.
            </p>
            <p>
              My goal is to give you the information and confidence you need to
              make good decisions—not to sell you services you don't need.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <Curve />
      </div>

      <article class="flow region wrapper">
        <h2>Let's Talk</h2>
        <p>
          Whether you need a quick code review or long-term strategic guidance,
          I'm here to help. First consultation is free — no obligation, no sales
          pitch.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/contact">Book Your Free Consultation</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
